==History ==
2019
*The Elixir Golem was once available in the [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Elixir Golem Draft Challenge]], which started on 11/10/2019. In this [[Tournament|challenge]], gameplay was similar to a regular Draft Challenge, except that one of the players was able to choose who would use the Elixir Golem. If the player achieved at least 8 wins, they obtained the Elixir Golem early.
*The Elixir Golem [[Cards|card]] was generally released on 4/11/2019. On the same day, a [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (4/11/2019)|Balance Update]], decreased the hitpoints of all of Elixir Golem's forms by 10%. It also moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Elixir Golem from Spooky Town to Electro Valley.
*On 26/11/2019, the [[Version History#End%20of%20November%202019%20Update%20(26/11/2019)|End of November 2019 Update]], added a card render to the Elixir Golem's card info screen.
*On 2/12/2019, a [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (2/12/2019)|Balance Update]], normalized the attack time interval of all Elixir Golem forms to 1.3 seconds. Being beneficial to the Elixir Golem and Elixir Golemites, but hurting the Elixir Blob damage per second significantly.
2020
*On 7/1/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (7/1/2020)|Balance Update]], decreased the hitpoints of all Elixir Golem forms by 6%.
2021
*On 7/6/2021, the [[Version History#Summer%202021%20Update%20(7/6/2021)|Summer 2021 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Elixir Golem from Electro Valley to Serenity Peak.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
2022
*On 2/8/2022, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (2/8/2022)|Balance Update]], increased the Elixir Golem's hitpoints by 9%, and the Elixir Golemites' hitpoints by 6%. It also increased the Elixir given by the Elixir Golem after being killed to 1 [[Elixir]] (from 0 Elixir), the Elixir given by the Elixir Golemite after being killed to 0.5 Elixir (from 0 Elixir), and decreased the Elixir given by the Elixir Blob after being killed to 0.5 Elixir (from 1 Elixir). The card description was also changed. It used to read "''Splits into two Elixir Golemites when destroyed, which split into two sentient Blobs when defeated. A Blob gives your opponent 1 Elixir when destroyed!''"
*On 4/10/2022, a [[Version History#Balance%20Changes%20(4/10/2022)|Balance Update]], decreased the attack time interval of all Elixir Golem forms to 1.1 seconds (from 1.3 seconds). Their first attack time interval was also increased to 0.8 seconds (from 1 second).
2023
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
*On 30/6/2023, a [[Version History#Maintenance%20Break%20(30/6/2023)|maintenance break]], fixed an issue where Elixir Golem was not giving Elixir to opponent when destroyed.
2025
*On 31/3/2025, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2025)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], increased the Elixir Golem's hitpoints by 0.06%, and decreased the Elixir Golemites' hitpoints by 0.13%. It also decreased the Elixir Golem's damage by 0.39%, increased the Elixir Golemites' damage by 0.78%, and increased the Elixir Blobs' damage by 1.58%. The same update also fixed a bug where Elixir Golemites and Elixir Blobs would not spawn after being buffed by [[Royal Chef]].

