==Trivia== 
*The word "''Golem''" occurs once in the Bible in Psalm 139:16, which uses the word "''golmi''", that means "my light form", "raw" material, connoting the unfinished human being. A golem is an animated, anthropomorphic being in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jewish_folklore Jewish folklore], which is entirely created from inanimate matter, usually clay or mud. The most famous golem narrative involves [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judah_Loew_ben_Bezalel Judah Loew ben Bezalel], the late 16th-century rabbi of Prague.
*The word “''Elixir''” comes from the Arabic word "اَلْإِكْسِير" (''al iksir''), which is the word for miracle substances. Dating back to the third century BC, Elixir was rumored to change base metals into gold and prolong life indefinitely.
*The Elixir Golem was designed after [https://youtu.be/aFrk-wDjJ4w?t=212 a scrapped concept], which involved a monster constructed entirely from [[Elixir]]. It was also originally called "Elixir Monster", and it would involve an Elixir Monster that would spawn Elixirmites when destroyed, Those Elixirmites would be fused back to an Elixir Monster if they were not defeated in time. This was later introduced with the C.H.A.O.S Epic Modifier From Blob to Glob.
*The Elixir Golem first made an appearance in an April Fool's image that Supercell posted in a [https://twitter.com/ClashRoyale/status/848110687012478976 Tweet], showing an 8v8 [[Basics of Battle|battle]].
*According to a Clash of Clans comment on [https://www.reddit.com/r/ClashOfClans/comments/l5hny0/ama_i_am_darian_community_manager_for_clash_of/gkua282/?context=3 Reddit], the Elixir Golem was prototyped during the development of TH12 in Clash of Clans. It would have gained strength as it creates destruction, and adopt the [[Rage]] [[:Category:Spell Cards|Spell]]'s characteristics when destroyed, similar to the [[Lumberjack]]. However, it was scrapped due to its complex mechanics.
*The Elixir Golem is 1 of 2 [[cards]] being associated with the Elixir mechanic, with the other being [[Elixir Collector]].
*The Elixir Golem is tied with the [[Super Lava Hound]] for the highest amount of forms and divisions of any card - it has 3 forms and divides 3 times.
*The Elixir Golem is one of the first troop cards to receive a card render, alongside the [[Archers]], [[Knight]], [[Goblins]], [[Bomber]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Bats]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Rascals]], [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Flying Machine]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Zappies]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], [[Balloon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], [[Lava Hound]], [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The Elixir Blobs are 1 of 9 troops that have the same sprite for both players, the others are Skeletons, [[Electro Spirit]], [[Fire Spirit]], Bats, [[Ice Spirit]], [[Heal Spirit]], [[Phoenix]], and Lava Pup.
*The Elixir Golem is 1 of 23 troops that has been featured in the [[Troop Rush]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being Skeletons, [[Skeleton Dragons]], Fire Spirit, Bats, [[Elite Barbarians]], [[Firecracker]], Rascal Girls, Royal Hogs, Heal Spirit, [[Guards]], Prince, Balloon, [[Golem]], Wall Breakers, Ram Rider, [[Sparky]], Phoenix, Royal Ghost, Bandit, Lumberjack, [[Santa Hog Rider]], and the [[Monk]].
*The Elixir Golem, along with the [[Minions]], Bomber, Skeletons, Skeleton Dragons, Ice Spirit, [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Mega Minion]], [[Ice Golem]], Dart Goblin, [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], [[Guards]], Baby Dragon, P.E.K.K.A, Giant Skeleton, Golem, Wall Breakers, Bowler, [[Executioner]], Mega Knight, [[Inferno Dragon]], Royal Ghost, and Lava Hound, are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Monsters monster] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*Unlike the Golem and Ice Golem, the Elixir Golem and its subsequent forms do not inflict death damage.
*According to the [https://youtu.be/zbVa7koGVQY?si=VH2WsCpNKobf9V8_ Season 4 trailer], the Elixir Golem originates from a meteor that came from outer space.
*The Elixir Golem is the subject of 4 [[Emotes]].
*Its [[Star Points|Star Level 1 skin]] has a different deploy sound effect to the one of an Elixir Golem without Star Levels.
*Despite the Damage Dealer [[Card Mastery]] task mentioning that the Elixir Golem can deal damage to troops or [[:Category:Building Cards|buildings]], it cannot progress the task by dealing damage to troops.
**The Elixir Golem is 1 of 6 troops that cannot deal damage to other troops whatsoever, the others being the [[Royal Giant]], Giant, Hog Rider, Royal Hogs, and [[Rune Giant]].

